direction: down

title: |md
  ## ECMP and multipath
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

setup: "Route has several nexthops" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  s_body: |md
    ```
    ip route add default \
     nexthop via 192.168.1.1 weight 1 \
     nexthop via 192.168.2.1 weight 1
    ```

    **Does:** one FIB result  
    carries multiple usable  
    next-hop candidates.
  |
}

hash: "Compute multipath hash" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  h_body: |md
    **Why:** pick one nexthop  
    per flow so packets do  
    not reorder across paths.

    Default policy **0**:  
    hash src IP + dst IP.

    Policy **1**: include L4  
    ports/proto for better  
    spread between the same  
    endpoint pair.
  |
}

select: "Select nexthop" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  sel_body: |md
    **Does:** maps hash into  
    weighted nexthop set.

    **Why next:** selected  
    nexthop provides output  
    device, gateway, MTU,  
    and neighbor lookup key.

    **State:** skb/rtable  
    has one chosen path.
  |
}

resilient: "Resilient hashing" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  rh_body: |md
    **Problem:** plain modulo  
    changes when a nexthop is  
    added/removed, so many  
    flows move.

    **Fix:** bucket table  
    remembers assignments;  
    removing one nexthop only  
    remaps its buckets.
  |
}

setup -> hash -> select -> resilient
